The original `may_list_ns()` and `do_listns_userns()` used `ns_capable_noaudit()` to grant listing access to any process with `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` in the target user namespace. This allowed privileged services (e.g., containers) to see namespaces owned by other services within the same user namespace, enabling information leakage between isolated entities. The check lacked any additional policy to restrict cross-service visibility based on ownership or other isolation boundaries.

